<.shell title="Forms" current={:forms}>
  <h1>Forms</h1>
  <p class="lead">Bold labels above, hints under them, errors on the field.</p>

  <h2>Which to use</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Text input: a short answer people type, such as a name.</li>
    <li>Select: one answer from a long list, such as a time zone.</li>
    <li>Radios: one answer from a few choices people should see side by side.</li>
    <li>
      Checkboxes: a yes or no setting in a form with a save button, or any number of things from a list.
    </li>
    <li>
      Switch: a setting with no save button, which changes the moment it's tapped. Inside a form with a save button, use a checkbox: a switch says the change already happened.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Text input</h2>
  <div class="demo">
    <.input id="e-name" name="e-name" label="Full name" value="Avery Chen" />
    <div class="max-w-xs">
      <.input id="e-email" name="e-email" type="email" label="Email" value="avery@example.com">
        SAR Duty sends the tax credit letter here.
      </.input>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="spec">
    Two widths: full, and <code>max-w-xs</code>
    (320px) for a short answer. Width follows the expected answer, not the page.
  </p>

  <h2>Select, date, and text area</h2>
  <div class="demo">
    <div class="max-w-xs">
      <.input
        id="e-kind"
        name="e-kind"
        type="select"
        label="Activity kind"
        options={["Incident", "Exercise", "Event"]}
        value="Incident"
      />
      <.input id="e-date" name="e-date" type="date" label="Start date" value="2025-09-28" />
    </div>
    <.input
      id="e-notes"
      name="e-notes"
      type="textarea"
      label="Notes"
      rows="3"
      value="Subject found at 21:10, walked out with the team."
    />
  </div>

  <h2>Read-only, disabled, and error</h2>
  <div class="demo">
    <div class="max-w-xs">
      <.input id="e-ro" name="e-ro" label="Latitude" value="49.7553" readonly>
        From D4H. Change it there.
      </.input>
      <.input id="e-dis" name="e-dis" label="Region" value="Canada" disabled />
      <.input
        id="e-err"
        name="e-err"
        label="Yard coordinate"
        value="49.7553 -123.131"
        errors={["Enter latitude and longitude separated by a comma"]}
      >
        Latitude and longitude, like 49.75533, -123.13110.
      </.input>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="spec">
    Read-only is for a value from D4H; the hint says where to change it. A field shows its error only after the person has typed in it or tried to save. See <a href={
      page_path(:fix_form_errors)
    }>Fix form errors</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Checkboxes</h2>
  <div class="demo">
    <.input
      id="e-refresh"
      name="e-refresh"
      type="checkbox"
      label="Refresh from D4H every night"
      checked
    >
      SAR Duty refreshes at 02:00.
    </.input>
    <fieldset>
      <legend>Activities to include</legend>
      <.hint>Meetings and public events count as events.</.hint>
      <label class="choice"><input type="checkbox" checked /> Incidents</label>
      <label class="choice"><input type="checkbox" checked /> Exercises</label>
      <label class="choice"><input type="checkbox" /> Events</label>
    </fieldset>
  </div>

  <p class="spec">
    24px boxes. Several that answer one question sit in a fieldset whose legend is the question, each in a <code>&lt;label class="choice"&gt;</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Radios</h2>
  <div class="demo">
    <fieldset>
      <legend>Hours to count</legend>
      <label class="choice"><input type="radio" name="e-hours" checked /> Primary and secondary</label>
      <label class="choice"><input type="radio" name="e-hours" /> Primary only</label>
    </fieldset>
  </div>

  <p class="spec">The checkbox list's markup, with radios. One answer, every choice in view.</p>

  <h2 id="switch">Switch</h2>
  <div class="demo">
    <div class="max-w-sm">
      <.switch id="e-sound" label="Sound" checked class="mb-4">A tone for each scan.</.switch>
      <.switch id="e-off" label="Off" class="mb-4" />
      <.switch id="e-disabled" label="Disabled" checked disabled class="mb-4" />
      <.switch id="e-focus" label="Keyboard focus" class="is-focus" />
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="spec">
    Label on the leading edge, switch on the trailing edge, a 48 by 28px track. Used on taking attendance at the door and the ID card check.
  </p>

  <h3>Compact switch</h3>
  <div class="demo">
    <div class="max-w-sm">
      <.button variant={:success} class="w-full">Scan ID cards</.button>
      <.switch id="e-compact" label="Sound" compact checked class="mt-2" />
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="spec">
    One page-level setting under the page's main action, such as Sound under the scan button. A small muted label and the switch, together on the trailing edge. No hint. The track stays full size, since it's tapped in a hurry.
  </p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Label md semibold. Hint sm muted. Error md bold in <code>--danger</code>. Input md.</li>
    <li>
      Inputs are 40px tall with a 2px border. Small inputs (32px, sm text) are for filter bars and editors inside a page, with
      <code>class="input-sm"</code>
      outside a filter bar.
    </li>
    <li>Fields are 24px apart.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <code>&lt;.input field=&#123;@form[:name]&#125; label="Full name"&gt;</code>, with the hint as its inner block.
      <code>type</code>
      picks select, date, textarea, password, or checkbox.
    </li>
    <li>
      A checkbox or radio list is a <code>&lt;fieldset&gt;</code>
      of <code>&lt;label class="choice"&gt;</code>
      inputs, as on the organization page.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>&lt;.switch id="…" label="…"&gt;</code>, with <code>compact</code> for the small one.
    </li>
  </ul>
</.shell>
